<!--
  What a SpawnItem key grants, where a retail capture shows it.

  SpawnItem (53064) carries a four character key, not an item id. The same
  function also summons pets, whose keys live in mobtemplate. No table in
  items.ocp, nanos.ocp, the database or the client ResourceDatabase maps these
  keys to items: none is an item or nano stat value in either byte order, and
  "LOMH" (HMOL as stored) occurs once in the whole client database, inside the
  package's own function arguments.

  Most rows below come from a capture of the package being opened: the
  server granted the items in the same order as the package lists its keys.
  The rest come from client data alone: a single-key package named
  "Vacuum Packed <name>" where exactly one item in the client has that name.
  Only keys whose item is unambiguous are recorded.

  Fan sites were checked on 2026-09-13 and add nothing: AUNO and aogalaxy show
  these keys as raw text ("User Summon Item HMOL"), aoitems.com no longer
  serves AO data, and Tinkerplants' data.json has no general items.

  Not recorded:
    VPPK  (303475) - grants a bag, sent as ChestItemFullUpdate; item id not
                     established.
    WK1Q, NTQL (248261) - two keys, four items granted
                     (20260909-141545 seq 2848-2855); which key gave which is
                     not determinable from one opening.
-->
<ItemSpawns>
